# CODEOWNERS
#
# Defines who must review pull requests for each part of the codebase.
# GitHub requests a review from these owners whenever a matching file is
# changed in a PR.  Combined with the branch protection rules configured
# in .github/workflows/branch-protection.yml, this ensures:
#
#   ✅ At least 1 approving review before any PR can be merged
#   ✅ The right people are automatically notified for each area
#
# Syntax: <pattern>  <owner> [<owner> ...]
#   - Patterns follow .gitignore glob rules, last match wins.
#   - Owners can be @username, @org/team, or user@email.com
#   - Replace the placeholder owners below with real GitHub usernames or teams.
#
# Docs: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default owner — catches everything not matched by a more specific rule.
# This guarantees that every PR has at least one required reviewer.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*                               @your-org/team-leads

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CI/CD & DevOps
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.github/                        @your-org/devops
.github/workflows/              @your-org/devops
.github/CODEOWNERS              @your-org/devops

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Application source
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
src/                            @your-org/frontend
src/_repositories/              @your-org/backend
src/_services/                  @your-org/backend
src/app/api/                    @your-org/backend

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database & migrations
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
prisma/                         @your-org/backend @your-org/dba

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tests
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
src/**/__tests__/               @your-org/qa
e2e/                            @your-org/qa

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Configuration & tooling
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
package.json                    @your-org/devops @your-org/team-leads
tsconfig.json                   @your-org/frontend
next.config.ts                  @your-org/frontend
eslint.config.mjs               @your-org/frontend
jest.config.ts                  @your-org/qa
playwright.config.ts            @your-org/qa
